&#xD;
Cooking instructions:
&#xD;
Pan Fry:&#xA0;Add 2 tablespoons of oil in a preheated skillet or saute pan. Place frozen Gyoza flat side down in pan and sear on medium high heat for 30 seconds. Add 5 tablespoons of water to pan. Turn heat to medium and cover. Steam Gyoza until water has evaporated and Gyoza is heated throughout, about 6 minutes. After water has evaporated, leave Gyoza in pan allowing the bottom to become brown and crispy, about 2 minutes. Serve immediately with your favorite dipping sauce.
&#xD;
Steaming:&#xA0;Add water to steamer or double boiler and wait until it boils. Place frozen Gyoza flat side down in steamer or double boiler. Steam for 7-10 minutes or until Gyoza are hot throughout. Serve immediately with your favorite soy or dipping sauce.

